' Written source: data-model.md (Expense), BR-08 to BR-11
title Expense Lifecycle\nFR-016, FR-020 to FR-024 (conditional draft: OC-1 open)

[*] --> Pending : create / active member\n[fields valid; at least one participant is not the creator]

Pending : status = PENDING
Pending : no balance effect (FR-020)
Pending : version increases on each edit

Approved : status = APPROVED
Approved : creates ledger entries (FR-026)
Approved : final

Rejected : status = REJECTED
Rejected : never affects balances
Rejected : final

Pending --> Pending : edit / creator only\n[expectedVersion matches; fields valid]\nshares recomputed; version + 1
Pending --> Approved : approve / eligible approver\n[expectedVersion matches]\nimmutable decision; creator notified
Pending --> Rejected : reject / eligible approver\n[expectedVersion matches; reason 1 to 200 characters]\nimmutable decision; creator notified with reason
Pending --> [*] : delete / creator only\n[expectedVersion matches]\nrow removed with shares and receipt;\nnotification links cleared

note left of Pending
  **Eligible approver:** participant, not the creator, active member.
  One decision settles the expense; the first recorded wins.
  Everyone referenced is active while Pending (INV-EXIT-2),
  so an eligible approver always exists.
end note

note bottom of Approved
  Approved and Rejected have no outgoing transitions: no edit,
  delete, or status change. Attempts get ConflictException(ALREADY_DECIDED).
  Rejected expenses are not resubmitted; create a new one (DEC-19).
end note

